<title>USA: IES sees 538 MW Iowa nuke fully back today.</title>
<headline>IES sees 538 MW Iowa nuke fully back today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>IES Utilities said Tuesday it expected its 538 megawatt (MW) Duane Arnold nuclear power station in Palo, Iowa, to reach full service later today after trimming its output following a recirculation pump trip.</p>
<p>&quot;It should be back to 100 percent by the end of today,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The company needed to repair a breaker that failed to close properly during testing and caused the recirculation pump to trip, he said.</p>
<p>IES Utilities is a subsidiary of IES Industries Inc.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
